    <field name="scopecontent_teim">Three wooden containers  made from timbers of the Zabriskie Homestead, Flatbush, Long Island. Donated to Erasmus Hall High School by Miss Louise Garvin Zabriskie. One canister (the one without a top) bears the stamped inscriptions &#34;J.L.Z. 1902,&#34; which indicates it (and its companions) was likely made in 1902, but the initials cannot stand for Dr. John L. Zabriskie, who died in 1895.</field>
